    "type": "question",
    "label": "57",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$x+\\sqrt{x-2}-2=0.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=2$.\n\nLet $u=\\sqrt{x-2}\\ge0$ and reject the negative substitute root.",
      "worked": "$x\\ge2$. Let $u=\\sqrt{x-2}\\ge0$, so $x=u^2+2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2+2+u-2&=0\\\\u^2+u&=0\\\\u(u+1)&=0\\\\u&=0\\text{ or }u=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $u=-1$. Thus $u=0$ and $x=2$. Check: $2+\\sqrt{2-2}-2=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 35
  },
